 '[{"text":"Renewable energy sources are always more reliable than fossil fuels","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Renewable energy availability can be inconsistent due to weather","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Fossil fuels never deplete","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Weather conditions have no effect on energy production","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The passage states that renewable sources'' availability "can be intermittent depending on weather conditions", directly supporting the inference about inconsistency due to weather.'),
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Reading Comprehension', 'hard', 'mcq',
