 null, 'Each term is double the previous term, so after 40 the next term is 40*2=80.'),
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Logical Reasoning and Analytical Ability', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'A is the son of B. C is the mother of A. What is the relationship between B and C?',
 '[{"text":"B and C are siblings","isCorrect":false},{"text":"B and C are spouses (husband and wife)","isCorrect":true},{"text":"B is the grandmother of C","isCorrect":false},{"text":"There is no possible relationship","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Since A is B''s son and C is A''s mother, B and C are both parents of A, making them spouses (assuming a standard two-parent family relationship).'),
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Logical Reasoning and Analytical Ability', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'In a certain code, "BOOK" is written as "CPPL". How is "PAGE" written in the same code?',
 '[{"text":"QBHF","isCorrect":true},{"text":"QBGF","isCorrect":false},{"text":"PBHF","isCorrect":false},{"text":"QAHF","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Each letter is shifted forward by one position in the alphabet (B to C, O to P, O to P, K to L); applying the same shift to P-A-G-E gives Q-B-H-F.'),

-- CSAT Paper II: Decision Making and Problem Solving
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Decision Making and Problem Solving', 'medium', 'mcq',
