 '[{"text":"Publicly confront the colleague during the meeting","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Speak to the colleague privately afterward to clarify the facts","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Say nothing and let it go permanently","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Complain to other colleagues informally","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Addressing the issue privately and calmly after the meeting allows for a professional resolution without creating public conflict, which is generally the most constructive first step.'),
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Decision Making and Problem Solving', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'As a team manager, if two team members have a conflict that is affecting their work, what should you do first?',
