 null, 'Understanding both perspectives individually before taking action ensures a fair, informed resolution, rather than acting on incomplete information.'),
('UPSC CSE (IAS)', 'CSAT (General Studies Paper II)', 'Decision Making and Problem Solving', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Which approach best exemplifies effective decision-making under conditions of uncertainty?',
 '[{"text":"Acting purely on instinct without considering evidence","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Weighing available evidence and potential outcomes before acting","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Delaying every decision indefinitely to avoid risk","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Following whatever the majority prefers, regardless of evidence","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Effective decision-making under uncertainty involves carefully weighing the available evidence and considering likely outcomes, rather than acting purely on instinct or avoiding the decision altogether.'),
